    "trivia": "- He is between his mid and late 30s.\n- **Darius**,  [Draven](https://wiki.leagueoflegends.com/en-us/Universe:Draven \"Universe:Draven\"),  [Invetia](https://wiki.leagueoflegends.com/en-us/Universe:Invetia_Varn \"Universe:Invetia Varn\"), and  [Quilletta Varn](https://wiki.leagueoflegends.com/en-us/Universe:Quilletta_Varn \"Universe:Quilletta Varn\") were all born in [Basilich](https://wiki.leagueoflegends.com/en-us/Basilich \"Basilich\").\n- \"*Darius isn't a crazed, bloodthirsty maniac but more of a cold-blooded killer moving through the battlefield with powerful, precise movements and striking with deadly force where it matters most. He takes pride in combat, but there's no primal bloodlust needing to be sated. Unpredictable sadists don't always make for the best commanders.*\" — [Harrow](https://wiki.leagueoflegends.com/en-us/Iain_%27Harrow%27_Hendry \"Iain 'Harrow' Hendry\"), narrative writer for Riot.[[6]](#cite_note-6)\n- Darius's *Trifarian Legion* is probably based on the [Triarii](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Triarii), the elite unit in the [Roman Republic](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roman_Republic)'s early period ​legions​s;\n  - The stem *Trifar-* is possibly based on [Latin](//en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classical_Latin) *trifārius* \"in three parts~places\" (cf. Sanskrit cognate त्रिधा *tridhā*), from PIE [*\\*tri-*](https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/tri-)[*dʰóh₁-*](https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/Reconstruction:Proto-Indo-European/d%CA%B0eh%E2%82%81-).[[7]](#cite_note-7)\n- Having been raised as an orphan, Darius doesn't care for titles or privileges—only to serve his empire through  [Noxian Might](https://wiki.leagueoflegends.com/en-us/Darius#Hemorrhage \"Darius\").[[8]](#cite_note-8)\n- His armor and axe were likely made with ore from the [Delverhold](https://wiki.leagueoflegends.com/en-us/Universe:The_Delverhold \"Universe:The Delverhold\") of the [Ironspike Mountains](https://wiki.leagueoflegends.com/en-us/Universe:Ironspike_Mountains \"Universe:Ironspike Mountains\").[[9]](#cite_note-9)",
    "role": "Unknown",
    "release_date": "Unknown"
  },
